.TH NOTTS 1 "2026-11-08" "holyc" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
notts \- notification daemon and sender
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B notts
.br
.B notts send
[\fB\-u\fR \fIlow|normal|critical\fR] [\fB\-t\fR \fIMS\fR] [\fB\-a\fR \fIAPP\fR] \fISUMMARY\fR [\fIBODY\fR]
.br
.B notts history
[\fIN\fR]
.br
.B notts last
.br
.B notts dnd on|off|status
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without arguments runs as the
.B org.freedesktop.Notifications
daemon on the session bus. It speaks the D\-Bus protocol itself and needs no libraries. Every notification is logged;
hooks and forwards can act on it. Stop other daemons (dunst, mako) first, only one may own the name.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B send
send a notification to whichever daemon runs; prints its id
.TP
.B history
the last N (default 20) notifications
.TP
.B last
the newest one, for a status bar
.TP
.B dnd
do\-not\-disturb: logged but silent, critical notifications always pass
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/notts/config
one "key value" per line: \fBhook\fR CMD (run with NOTTS_ID, NOTTS_APP, NOTTS_SUMMARY, NOTTS_BODY, NOTTS_URGENCY),
\fBdiscord\fR WEBHOOK_URL, \fBtelegram\fR TOKEN CHAT_ID, \fBignore\fR APP. Discord and Telegram need curl.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/notts/history
tab separated log.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/notts.last
newest notification.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR notify-send (1),
.BR shot (1)
